  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers tonight, cooler and dry on Friday in the \nwake of the cold front.\n\nShowers are developing across southern Ontario this afternoon and \nwill be seeing an overall increase in coverage as they gradually \nwork their way southeastward ahead of a cold front. Overall, QPF on \nthe lighter side, and the main forecast question will be the \npotential for any embedded lightning. As of this issuance, no \nthunder in the forecast due to a marked lack of instability, but \nthe chances, although very low, are non-zero given some moderate \nlow/mid level flow. Showers exit after 05Z to the southeast with \nlingering low level clouds through the morning hours Friday. Cooler \nairmass filters in behind the cold front as high pressure builds \nback into the southern Great Lakes region for the end of the week \nand into the weekend. Temperatures will make a rebound back to above \nnormal for the end of the weekend into early next week in dry \nweather as the warmer weather pattern remains in overall\ncontrol.",
